.TH XD\-SEARCH 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-search \- Search for Files or Folders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-search
.RI [ folder ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-search
is Windows 2000's Search for Files or Folders, from the Start menus'
Search items and F3 in
.BR xd\-files (1).
It finds files by name (with
.B *
and
.B ?
wildcards) or by text inside them, under the folder in Look in, and lists
them with their folder, size, type and date; double-clicking one opens it.
Links aren't followed, and hidden files and folders are skipped.
.PP
.I folder
starts in Look in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-files (1),
.BR find (1)
